-- je54-art09-10-references: Articles 9 and 10 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, for a given TEXT of the Law.
-- Article 9 (references to enactments) is the same in all seven deposited texts except for 9(3), which in V1 reads "as amended from time to time" and from V2a (28 September 2021) reads "as amended, revised or
-- otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time".  Article 10 is the same in all seven.  A question about a day before 1 January 2019 refuses (no text is deposited).
-- Selecting date: the day the reference is read (the day the fact occurred), supplied by the caller as the text v; the date of the passing or making of an enactment, where the Article needs one, is a separate input.
-- This module does not encode the 2021 Law: "revised or otherwise consolidated" is a form named by the input, and its meaning is in that Law.

§ `Article 9: Construction of references to enactments`

-- src:41 | (1) A reference in a Law to a Part, Article or Schedule by number only and without further identification is a reference to the Part, Article or Schedule of that number in that Law.
-- src:42 | (2) A reference in an Article or other division of a Law to a paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause by number or letter only and without further identification is a reference to the paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause of that number or letter in the Article or other division of that Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(1) and 9(2) (src:41-42)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 9(1) and 9(2): only a reference by number or letter alone is dealt with` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 9(1) and 9(2) deal only with a reference by number or letter only and without further identification"

-- src:41 | (1) A reference in a Law to a Part, Article or Schedule by number only and without further identification is a reference to the Part, Article or Schedule of that number in that Law.
-- src:42 | (2) A reference in an Article or other division of a Law to a paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause by number or letter only and without further identification is a reference to the paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause of that number or letter in the Article or other division of that Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(1) and 9(2) (src:41-42)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 9: the Article does not say whether it applies to something that is not an enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 9 applies to enactments (Article 9(5)); it does not say whether it applies to something that is not an enactment"

-- 9(1): a reference in a Law to a Part, Article or Schedule by number only is to the Part, Article or Schedule of that number in that Law.
-- 9(2): a reference in an Article or other division of a Law to a paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause by number or letter only is to the one of that number or letter in the Article or other division of that Law.
-- 9(4): both apply, with the necessary changes, in a subordinate enactment.  The necessary changes are the substitution of the subordinate enactment for the Law.
-- src:41 | (1) A reference in a Law to a Part, Article or Schedule by number only and without further identification is a reference to the Part, Article or Schedule of that number in that Law.
-- src:42 | (2) A reference in an Article or other division of a Law to a paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause by number or letter only and without further identification is a reference to the paragraph, sub-paragraph, clause or sub-clause of that number or letter in the Article or other division of that Law.
-- src:44 | (4) This Article shall apply, with the necessary changes, to a subordinate enactment as it applies to a Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(1), 9(2) and 9(4) (src:41-42), (src:44)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      r IS A `Reference by number or letter`
GIVETH A `Place referred to`
`Article 9(1) and 9(2): the place that a reference by number or letter alone leads to` v r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF r's `further identification is given` THEN `Article 9(1) and 9(2): only a reference by number or letter alone is dealt with`
           IF r's `the kind of instrument that contains the reference` EQUALS `something that is none of these` THEN `Article 9: the Article does not say whether it applies to something that is not an enactment`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER r's `the kind of division named`
               WHEN `a Part` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a Part`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the instrument that contains the reference`
               WHEN `an Article` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `an Article`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the instrument that contains the reference`
               WHEN `a Schedule` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a Schedule`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the instrument that contains the reference`
               WHEN `a paragraph` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a paragraph`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the division that contains the reference`
               WHEN `a sub-paragraph` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a sub-paragraph`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the division that contains the reference`
               WHEN `a clause` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a clause`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the division that contains the reference`
               WHEN `a sub-clause` THEN `Place referred to` WITH
                   `the kind of division` IS `a sub-clause`
                   `the number or letter` IS r's `the number or letter given`
                   `the place it is in` IS r's `the division that contains the reference`

-- 9(3): "Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended [V1: from time to time] [V2: revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning
-- of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time] and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law."
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:43 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:40 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[10]
-- src:43 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[11]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:43), (src:l_17_1954_20220130:40), (src:43)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 9(3): the context otherwise requires, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "the context otherwise requires: Article 9(3) does not say what the reference is then to"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:43 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(3), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:43)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 9(3): the text before 28 September 2021 does not say revised or otherwise consolidated` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 9(3) as it read before 28 September 2021 says amended from time to time and does not say revised or otherwise consolidated"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:43 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.
-- src:l_17_1954_20220130:40 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[10]
-- src:l_17_1954_20220831:41 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[10]
-- src:l_17_1954_20240110:42 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[10]
-- src:l_17_1954_20251123:42 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[11]
-- src:l_17_1954_20260618:42 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[11]
-- src:43 | (3) Unless the context otherwise requires, a reference in a Law to an enactment is a reference to that enactment as amended, revised or otherwise consolidated (within the meaning of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) from time to time and includes a reference to that enactment as extended or applied under another enactment, including another provision of that Law.[11]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:43), (src:l_17_1954_20220130:40), (src:l_17_1954_20220831:41), (src:l_17_1954_20240110:42), (src:l_17_1954_20251123:42), (src:l_17_1954_20260618:42), (src:43)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      form IS A `Form in which an enactment is meant`
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` v form `the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN `Article 9(3): the context otherwise requires, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER form
               WHEN `the enactment as amended` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the enactment as extended or applied under another enactment` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the enactment as extended or applied under another provision of the same Law` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` THEN
                   CONSIDER v
                   WHEN `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021` THEN `Article 9(3): the text before 28 September 2021 does not say revised or otherwise consolidated`
                   OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 9(6): "subordinate enactment" means an enactment passed or made under a Law or under the authority of an Order in Council.
-- src:46 | (6) In this Article, “subordinate enactment” means an enactment passed or made under a Law or under the authority of an Order in Council.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(6) (src:46)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of an Order in Council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 9(4) and 9(5): "This Article shall apply, with the necessary changes, to a subordinate enactment as it applies to a Law.  This Article shall apply to all enactments, including this Law, whenever passed or made."
-- The day on which the enactment was passed or made is accepted and ignored: that no date matters is the whole of 9(5).
-- src:44 | (4) This Article shall apply, with the necessary changes, to a subordinate enactment as it applies to a Law.
-- src:45 | (5) This Article shall apply to all enactments, including this Law, whenever passed or made.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 9(4) and 9(5) (src:44-45)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      k IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the day on which the enactment was passed or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `How Article 9 applies to an instrument`
`Article 9(4) and 9(5): how the Article applies to an enactment passed or made on any day` v k `the day on which the enactment was passed or made` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF k EQUALS `something that is none of these` THEN `Article 9: the Article does not say whether it applies to something that is not an enactment`
           IF `Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` k THEN `with the necessary changes, the instrument being a subordinate enactment`
           OTHERWISE `as it stands, the instrument being a Law`

§ `Article 10: Construction of subordinate enactments`

-- "Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this
-- Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power."
-- The commencement of this Law is 21 August 1954 (Table of Legislation History).  A day before it is not "after the commencement"; a later day is.  The Law gives no time of day for its own commencement (Article 1(5)
-- and 1(6) were inserted in 2003 and cannot fix when the Law itself began), so on 21 August 1954 itself the Article cannot say whether an enactment passed that day was passed after the commencement.
-- src:47 | 10 Construction of subordinate enactments
-- src:48 | Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 10 (src:47-48)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 10: the Article deals only with an enactment that confers power to pass another` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 10 deals only where an enactment confers power to pass another enactment"

-- src:47 | 10 Construction of subordinate enactments
-- src:48 | Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 10 (src:47-48)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 10: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 10 does not say what the expressions then mean"

-- src:47 | 10 Construction of subordinate enactments
-- src:48 | Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 10 (src:47-48)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 10: the Law does not say at what time of day it came into operation` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Law gives no time of day for its own commencement on 21 August 1954, so Article 10 cannot say whether an enactment passed that day was passed after it"

-- src:47 | 10 Construction of subordinate enactments
-- src:48 | Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 10 (src:47-48)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 10: an enactment passed before the commencement of the Law is not dealt with` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"

-- src:47 | 10 Construction of subordinate enactments
-- src:48 | Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers power to pass any other enactment, expressions used in that other enactment if it is passed after the commencement of this Law, shall, unless the contrary intention appears, have the same respective meanings as in the enactment conferring the power.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 10 (src:47-48)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers power to pass the other enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the other enactment was passed` IS A DATE
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` v `the enactment confers power to pass the other enactment` `the day on which the other enactment was passed` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers power to pass the other enactment` THEN `Article 10: the Article deals only with an enactment that confers power to pass another`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 10: a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           IF `the day on which the other enactment was passed` EQUALS `the day on which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force` THEN `Article 10: the Law does not say at what time of day it came into operation`
           IF `the day on which the other enactment was passed` LESS THAN `the day on which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force` THEN `Article 10: an enactment passed before the commencement of the Law is not dealt with`
           OTHERWISE TRUE
